<p>This chapter finally solved a problem I’d been chasing for a long time: how to pick elements in 3D space from a 2D screen. The core idea is a technique called <strong>3D ray-object intersection</strong>.</p>

<p>Besides this approach, there’s also one that <strong>uses a color/object ID to determine which object was clicked</strong>.</p>

